# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore — Reverse Document Generator (Flask Application)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file controls what is excluded from the Docker build context when the
# Dockerfile executes `COPY . .` (see Dockerfile line ~225). The Flask
# application image must contain ONLY runtime artifacts:
#   * app/                    — Flask blueprints, services, utils (RUNTIME)
#   * lib/reverse_document/   — LangGraph pipeline library (RUNTIME)
#   * wsgi.py, run.py         — application entry points (RUNTIME)
#   * find_trace_runs.py      — trace correlation utility (RUNTIME)
#   * requirements.txt        — dependency manifest (BUILD)
#   * Dockerfile, Makefile    — build/deploy automation (build-time only;
#                               harmless if copied into the image)
#
# The patterns below exclude version-control metadata, local secrets,
# Python build/cache artifacts, virtual environments, test suites, IDE
# configuration, OS metadata, log files, and developer credential files —
# all of which would otherwise inflate the image and risk leaking
# secrets or development-only behavior into production.
#
# CRITICAL: Do NOT add patterns that match `app/`, `lib/`, `wsgi.py`,
# `run.py`, `requirements.txt`, or `find_trace_runs.py` — those paths
# contain runtime code required by the Gunicorn-served Flask service.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control metadata and local environment overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and compiled artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python virtual environments (developer-local; never shipped in image)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
env/
venv/
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test artifacts and CI-only directories — tests run in CI, not in the
# deployed Cloud Run Service. Excluding these keeps the production image
# small and prevents accidental execution of test code in production.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / Editor configuration files (developer-local only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development service-account keys and CI credential files —
# these MUST NEVER be baked into a container image. Credentials are
# injected at runtime via Cloud Run service-account bindings or, at
# build time, via BuildKit's `--mount=type=secret` flag (see Dockerfile
# line ~216 where GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is mounted, not COPY'd).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
service-key-*.json
gha-creds-*.json
